{"type":"standard","title":"Michael Baumgartner","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Michael Baumgartner</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q6828508","titles":{"canonical":"Michael_Baumgartner","normalized":"Michael Baumgartner","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Michael Baumgartner</span></span>"},"pageid":33285482,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Congressman_Michael_Baumgartner_%28cropped%29.png/330px-Congressman_Michael_Baumgartner_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":395},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5c/Congressman_Michael_Baumgartner_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":505,"height":604},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1378002719","tid":"c495ab83-be50-11f1-9350-a32178ca577d","timestamp":"2026-10-02T11:02:33Z","description":"American politician (born 1975)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Baumgartner","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Baumgartner?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Baumgartner?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Michael_Baumgartner"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Baumgartner","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Michael_Baumgartner","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Baumgartner?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Michael_Baumgartner"}},"extract":"Michael James Baumgartner is an American politician and former diplomat serving as the U.S. representative from Washington's 5th congressional district since 2025. Previously, he served as the 28th Spokane County treasurer from 2019 to 2025 and as a member of the Washington State Senate from 2011 to 2019, representing the 6th district. He is a member of the Republican Party.","extract_html":"<p><b>Michael James Baumgartner</b> is an American politician and former diplomat serving as the U.S. representative from Washington's 5th congressional district since 2025. Previously, he served as the 28th Spokane County treasurer from 2019 to 2025 and as a member of the Washington State Senate from 2011 to 2019, representing the 6th district. He is a member of the Republican Party.</p>"}